# CSS modules (feature components)

## One stylesheet per component folder

- Prefer a **local `s.module.less`** (or `.module.scss`) **next to the component** that uses it, imported as **`./s.module.less`** (or a short relative path within that folder).
- **Avoid** a single mega-stylesheet shared by every file under a feature via long relative imports (`../../s.module.less`). Split so each **component folder** owns its styles; easier ownership and dead-style detection.

## Shared snippets across components

- If the same small rule (e.g. icon + tooltip spacing) appears in multiple places, **duplicating** a few lines across modules is acceptable when it keeps **co-location** clear.
- Promote to a **shared** module only when many unrelated features need the same token or utility class (follow existing design-system / `_shared` patterns if present).

## Naming

- Keep using the project’s existing CSS-module **class naming**; this skill only governs **file placement** and **import distance**, not BEM vs camelCase.

## Structure inside the file

- **Nest** rules so selectors follow the **component DOM tree** (parents wrap children in the `.less` file the same way as in JSX). That makes ownership of styles obvious at a glance.
- Rely on structure instead of long explanatory comments; keep **comments minimal** unless documenting a non-obvious override (e.g. third-party widget).
